      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T21:51:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Or are we using a bad voltage request for the case where the battery isn\u0027t there?  Should the calling code for charge_request be the one changing here for the no-battery case?\n\nIt was this. Our charger sets regulation in steps of 64mV compared to others with 8mV or so. So charge_request ended up getting called with paramters 64, and -1 which totally skipped that entire clause and brought down VSYS.\n\nAs to the reason for that, it may be that our AC presence criteria is incorrect/unreliable? See also around L2019.",
      "parentUuid": "e660eedf_972315d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1216,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1216,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "c36d91ecaa9e9253198919305c8dedb4effb6a1b",
